// Title: Potential Rundll32 Execution With DLL Stored In ADS
// Sigma ID: 9248c7e1-2bf3-4661-a22c-600a8040b446
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Harjot Singh, '@cyb3rjy0t'
// Date: 2023-01-21 | Modified: 2026-03-16
// ATT&CK: stealth, T1564.004
// Description: Detects execution of rundll32 where the DLL being called is stored in an Alternate Data Stream
//   (ADS).
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Rundll32
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_rundll32_ads_stored_dll_execution.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\rundll32.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "RUNDLL32.EXE") and ProcessCommandLine matches regex "[Rr][Uu][Nn][Dd][Ll][Ll]32(?:\\.[Ee][Xx][Ee])? \\S+?\\w:\\S+?:"
